// links still land.
---

<section class="band" id="use-cases">
  <span id="solutions"></span>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band-head">
      <h2>Four things people build with Turf.</h2>
      <p>From a GPU cloud to a product that installs itself: the same engine, the same plan, the
        same approval points.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="solutions four">
      <div class="sol">
        <span class="tagline">Neocloud providers</span>
        <h3>GPU clouds, from metal to tokens</h3>
        <p>Pools of inventory to a certified cluster and a served model, in one run, and day 2 on the
          provider’s runbook.</p>
        <a class="runit" href="/use-cases/#gpu-clouds">metal to tokens →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="sol">
        <span class="tagline">SaaS and platform providers</span>
        <h3>Managed services on Kubernetes fleets</h3>
        <p>A control plane, a golden recipe, and a fleet of tenant clusters, each its own stack under
          approval.</p>
        <a class="runit" href="/use-cases/#kubernetes-fleets">one recipe, many clusters →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="sol">
        <span class="tagline">ISVs and AI-native products</span>
        <h3>Products that install themselves</h3>
        <p>The reference architecture as modules, planned in the customer’s account, with the
          installer’s own steps as turf actions.</p>
        <a class="runit" href="/use-cases/#installers">ship the installer →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="sol">
        <span class="tagline">Teams adopting agents</span>
        <h3>The ultimate infrastructure agent</h3>
        <p>Skills, state tools, provider schemas and the planfile for policy, designed for efficient
          reasoning models.</p>
        <a class="runit" href="/use-cases/#agents">the agent’s toolkit →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
